# save: 10-ToThreed
# Sweep segment 10 -> 11: the Twoson hotel phone, the Runaway Five (Yes) and their bus to Threed,
# the cemetery (No Good Fly + Smelly Ghost: Ness PSI Rockin alpha, Paula PSI Fire alpha), the
# gatekeepers' area (flag 46), the Sunset Hotel (the girl, the corridor room: the zombie
# capture), the jail, then Jeff in Winters. Recorded in chunks with playtest/sweep/rec.py
# late-pads: the port replays the pads the original read after each lag-merged frame
# Doors: skip K / lag (emu frame of K+20) / ignore: idle K+30; idle 14741 is the post-battle
# fade-in. The Sunset Hotel's street door spends 3 more CPU-time frames in the original (the
# emu's LSTEP steps by 2 through the load: lags 17036-17038); the lobby -> corridor fade-in
# ends 4 frames later there (idle 17269-17272)
